---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { LINKS } from '../consts';
---

<Base title="About" description="About The Voyager and the AI architect behind it.">
	<article class="prose">
		<p class="eyebrow">About</p>
		<h1>About The Voyager</h1>

		<h2>What this blog is about</h2>
		<p>
			AI is moving faster than anyone can read. The Voyager is where I sort the signal from the noise, for
			architects, engineers and anyone building with LLMs.
		</p>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<a href="/brief/">☕ Daily Brief</a>: the few AI stories each morning that actually matter, and what they
				mean if you design systems. Five minutes, then get on with your day.
			</li>
			<li>
				<a href="/deep-dives/">🔭 Deep Dives</a>: one topic a day, explained properly: models and agents, new
				research, system design, interviews, open-source projects and weekend builds.
			</li>
			<li>
				<a href="/writing/">✍️ Writing</a>: my own essays on what I'm building and where LLM architecture is
				heading.
			</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			The Brief and Deep Dives are <a href="/disclosure/">curated with AI</a> and clearly labelled. Writing is
			all mine. If something here saves you an hour or sparks an idea, that's the whole point.
		</p>

		<!-- TODO: write this section in your own words. -->
		<h2>Who I am</h2>
		<p class="todo">
			A few sentences about you: what you do, what you've built, and what you're working toward as an AI
			architect.
		</p>

		<h2>Find me</h2>
		<ul class="links">
			<li><a href={LINKS.github}>GitHub: VRSupriya</a></li>
			<li><a href={LINKS.substack}>Substack: The Voyager newsletter</a></li>
			<li>
				{LINKS.linkedin ? <a href={LINKS.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a> : <span class="todo">LinkedIn (link coming soon)</span>}
			</li>
		</ul>
	</article>
</Base>

<style>
	.todo {
		padding: 0.8rem 1rem;
		border: 1px dashed var(--amber);
		border-radius: 10px;
		color: var(--muted);
		background: var(--amber-soft);
	}
	li .todo {
		display: inline-block;
		padding: 0.1rem 0.5rem;
	}
</style>
